  {
   "messageId": 1,
   "question": "Thinking over your life up to now, which two or three times were the fullest or hardest, and roughly which years?",
   "words": "The one that stands out is the year Dad lost his job, when I was 14. The cannery closed, he sat out in the truck for hours, Mom and Dad fought every night, and I more or less stopped eating until he found the delivery job. I was small when Grandpa lost the orchard, and I wonder whether that did something to all of us. I also wonder what moving west did to Dad's family before I was born."
  }
